{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Of the Jeminites.</b> Do not seek precision in the names, and likewise from פוני [Punon-ites] and from לשפופם [the Shuphamites]: the Shuphamite, the Jeminite, the family of the Jaminites — it is not הימיני as in the case of מן בריעה בריעי [from Bria, the Brite]. וחגי and שוני are missing the yod of relation; or: this is the yod of relation and that of the name is missing — and this is the correct view. After Reuben, Simeon, and Gad — who camp alongside it — only Manasseh precedes Ephraim, whereas at the wilderness of Sinai it is reversed. The correct explanation is that this is on account of their number, for the children of Ephraim exceeded the children of Manasseh in the wilderness of Sinai by eight thousand three hundred, while in the plains of Moab the children of Manasseh exceed the children of Ephraim by twenty thousand two hundred. Likewise it records for the families of Benjamin five sons: Bela, Ashbel, Ahiram, Shephupham, and Hupham."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The Hebrew lists Benjamin's sons as בכר וגרא ונעמן וראש וארד, which do not match the standard biblical forms (בלע, אשבל, אחירם, שפופם, חופם); translated as written. The phrase וחגי may be a corruption or truncated example; rendered as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:38.257804696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}